ecutor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both contractual outcomes are satisfied. The independent restart protocol is complete: node1 had a pre-restart boot identity and healthy scheduler/task state, the restart was acknowledged, a different boot identity was observed afterward and independently confirmed by lifecycle evidence, and the scheduler, cron entry, retained log data, and command output recovered successfully.","limitations":["No naturally timed 02:15 cron invocation was captured; scheduling is established by the exact cron entry, active/enabled crond service, and successful cron-like executions.","Package-health collection timed out in both lifecycle snapshots, so package consistency could not be independently assessed.","The node clock changed substantially across the restart, producing an August timestamp before restart and an October timestamp afterward; this does not contradict the demonstrated append behavior or persistence."]}
